# Select with Search

### 1. Single selection

The single-select component must follow a simple, clear and compact design:

- The field displays the currently selected value with a chevron indicating that it can be opened.
- On click, a dropdown menu opens directly below the field.
- The menu has a distinct, clean and readable surface.
- Each option is displayed on a separate line with consistent alignment.
- The selected option is identifiable by a check icon (✓) placed on the left.

### 2. Multiple selection

- The multiple selection uses the same visual language as the single selection.
- Each option has a square selection checkbox on the left.
- The box is empty when an option is not selected and checked when it is.
- Several options can be selected simultaneously.

### 3. Selection with search

For lists containing many options, the menu must include a search bar.

- The search bar is integrated at the top of the menu, above the list of options.
- The input dynamically filters the displayed options.
- Only the options matching the search are displayed.
- If no result matches, show an explicit empty state.
- The search must work with both single selection and multiple selection.

